    "pdpPlainTextPreview": "First sovereign to pair King Charles III's definitive effigy with the classic St George and dragon reverse\nWE ARE STRENGTHENING ACCOUNT SECURITY AND PROTECTING YOUR ACCESS WITH 2 STEP VERIFICATION. FIND OUT MORE Home Sovereign All Sovereign Coins 2024 Proof Sovereign Share via Gold Proof 2024 Proof Sovereign Low Mintage of 9250 Price: £1,260.00 EMAIL ME WHEN IN STOCK Email Me When In Stock PRODUCT CODE: HIS24PS First sovereign to pair King Charles III's definitive effigy with the classic St George and dragon reverse Marks the return of Pistrucci's iconic design after the 2023 coronation special reverse Martin Jennings' left-facing portrait of His Majesty, the first standard issue under the new Carolean era Proof finish contrasts frosted devices with mirror-polished fields for exceptional clarity and depth Positioned as the foundational date of the ongoing Charles III sovereign sequence Finely milled edge and precision-struck legends uphold modern Royal Mint proof standards Certified authenticity from The Royal Mint Gold Proof Read the full description YOU MIGHT ALSO BE INTERESTED IN ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2026 1oz Silver Bullion Coin £62.52 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2022 1 oz Silver Bullion Coin £61.32 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 5 Genius Medal £9.95 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2026 1oz Gold Bullion Coin £3,487.00 In Stock ADD TO BASKET 100th Anniversary of the Birth of Queen Elizabeth II 2026 UK £5 Brilliant Uncirculated Coin £17.50 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2026 1oz Silver Bullion Twenty-Five Coin Tube £1,483.00 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 4 Mastermind Medal £9.95 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 1g Gold Bullion Minted Bar £140.78 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 3 Decoder Medal £9.95 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 2 Explorer Medal and Collector Folder £9.95 In Stock Struck in honour of a new Carolean era, the 2024 Gold Proof Sovereign is the first sovereign to pair the definitive portrait of His Majesty King Charles III with the classic St George and the dragon reverse. Following the specially designed reverse of the 2023 coronation-dated issue, this coin marks a return to the long‑standing sovereign tradition while signalling the beginning of a new chapter for Britain’s most famous gold coin. The obverse features Martin Jennings’ left‑facing effigy of King Charles III, presented without a crown in keeping with long‑standing numismatic convention. The finely modelled portrait, surrounded by the Latin legend naming Charles as king, is brought into sharp focus by the proof finish, which contrasts frosted relief with deeply polished fields. For collectors of modern British coinage, this is the first standard‑reverse sovereign to bear His Majesty’s definitive likeness, giving it a natural place at the head of any Carolean date run. On the reverse, Benedetto Pistrucci’s iconic St George and the dragon returns after its absence on the 2023 coronation design, reasserting the motif that has come to define the sovereign over more than two centuries. The rearing horse, flowing cloak and defeated dragon are rendered with exceptional clarity, every detail of the classic engraving heightened by the proof strike. The 2024 date in the exergue firmly anchors this piece as the point where the traditional reverse resumes under a new monarch, creating an important link between the Elizabethan and Carolean series. For the numismatist, the 2024 Gold Proof Sovereign offers a number of compelling attractions: it is the first year in which the regular‑type sovereign unites King Charles III’s definitive effigy with the canonical St George and the dragon reverse; it follows directly on from a one‑year‑only special reverse; and it stands at the very beginning of the ongoing Carolean sovereign sequence. As such, it forms a distinguished and historically resonant addition to any cabinet devoted to the story of the sovereign and the evolving portraiture of Britain’s kings and queens. SPECIFICATION Specification Value Denomination Soverei"
